cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "yesand: rewriting agent instructions into positive form"
message: "If you use yesand or its benchmark, please cite this repository."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Verschuur
    given-names: Ben
repository-code: "https://github.com/sem-sea/SayYes"
url: "https://github.com/sem-sea/SayYes"
abstract: >-
  yesand is an Agent Skill that rewrites instructions and prompts into positive
  form, so each line names the action to take rather than a prohibition to
  remember, while preserving genuine safety refusals verbatim. The repository
  ships a reproducible compliance benchmark of 41 paired instructions across 19
  deterministically checkable constraint types, designed after IFEval, for
  measuring whether positively phrased instructions are followed more reliably
  than negatively phrased ones of identical meaning.
keywords:
  - prompt engineering
  - agent skills
  - instruction following
  - negation
  - large language models
  - benchmark
license: MIT
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-08-27"
